<section class="page-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">DELIVERY AT A GLANCE</div><h1>CI / CD<span class="heading-period">.</span></h1><p>Build and deployment activity from your repositories.</p></div><span class="integration-badge <%= configured?'connected':'disconnected' %>"><span></span><%= configured?'GitHub connected':'GitHub not configured' %></span></section>
<% if (!configured) { %><div class="integration-setup"><div class="integration-art"><i class="bi bi-github"></i></div><div class="eyebrow">REPOSITORY INTEGRATION</div><h2>Your delivery signals, in one view.</h2><p>Connect a GitHub account by setting <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> and <code>GITHUB_OWNER</code> in your Vercel environment variables. Tokens stay on the server and are never sent to the browser.</p><div class="integration-steps"><span><b>01</b> Create a GitHub token with Actions read access</span><span><b>02</b> Add the two variables to Vercel</span><span><b>03</b> Redeploy to load recent workflow runs</span></div><span class="demo-label"><i class="bi bi-info-circle"></i> Live data will appear after configuration. No sample runs are shown.</span></div><% } else { %><div class="pipeline-configured panel"><span class="integration-art"><i class="bi bi-github"></i></span><h2>GitHub is connected</h2><p>Choose a repository to inspect its recent workflow runs.</p><form id="pipeline-search" class="inline-search"><input name="repository" required placeholder="repository-name"><button class="button button-primary">Load runs</button></form><div id="pipeline-results"></div></div><% } %>
